- ### Evolution
+ ### Évolution

- A diff compares two versions. An *evolution* follows each element through many. A value which is
- in the first version and the last is recognized as the same value, even if it disappeared and
- came back in between:
+ Un diff compare deux versions. Une *évolution* suit chaque élément à travers de nombreuses
+ versions. Une valeur présente dans la première version et dans la dernière est reconnue comme
+ la même valeur, même si elle a disparu puis est revenue entre les deux :

= came back in between:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val versions = List(List('d', 'o', 'g'), List('c', 'a', 't'), List('d', 'o', 'g'))
+ val versions = List(List('d', 'o', 'g'), List('c', 'a', 't'), List('d', 'o', 'g'))

- val evolution = evolve(versions)
+ val evolution = evolve(versions)

= val evolution = evolve(versions)
- ```
+ ```

- Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
+ Chaque version est désignée par un ordinal, et est reconstruite exactement telle qu'elle était :

= Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(evolution(Ter).inspect)
+ Out.println(evolution(Ter).inspect)

= Out.println(evolution(Ter).inspect)
- ```
+ ```

- This is the structure which a document history, an undo stack or a series of drafts needs.
+ C'est la structure dont ont besoin un historique de document, une pile d'annulation ou une
+ série de brouillons.

